  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "rd_c",
      "defType": "meta/comment",
      "position": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": -264
      },
      "params": {
        "text": "Reaction–diffusion\n\nThe Simulation node's `reaction` mode runs Gray–Scott chemistry: chemical B eats A and spreads, A is fed back in, B is killed off, and the balance (`preset`, or `custom` feed and kill) decides the pattern — coral, mitosis, fingerprints, worms, maze, spots, waves.\n\nB starts where the `seed image` is bright: here the word, rasterised, so the coral grows out of the letters. `colors` ramp from no B to the most. Click the Bang to start over, or switch the preset.",
        "width": 520,
        "height": 200
      },
      "portValues": {
        "text": "Reaction–diffusion\n\nThe Simulation node's `reaction` mode runs Gray–Scott chemistry: chemical B eats A and spreads, A is fed back in, B is killed off, and the balance (`preset`, or `custom` feed and kill) decides the pattern — coral, mitosis, fingerprints, worms, maze, spots, waves.\n\nB starts where the `seed image` is bright: here the word, rasterised, so the coral grows out of the letters. `colors` ramp from no B to the most. Click the Bang to start over, or switch the preset.",
        "width": 520,
        "height": 200
      }
    },
